      "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\n`test_depyf_integration` forks its test process on CUDA, so it fails with `Cannot re-initialize CUDA in forked subprocess` whenever an earlier test in the same pytest session has initialized CUDA. This runs it in a spawned process instead, as ROCm already does. Needed before vllm-project/ci-infra#888 merges: that PR changes how PyTorch Fullgraph is sharded, and its new plan puts such a test first in the same session.\n\n## Claims\n\n- `test_depyf_integration` passes no matter which tests run before it in the session.\n- No other test changes: one decorator argument.\n\n## Validation\n\n- **Without the fix:** staging build [99301](https://buildkite.com/vllm/ci/builds/99301) (ci-infra#888's sharding plan): PyTorch Fullgraph shard 5/7 ran `test_clone_elimination.py`, then `test_depyf_integration` failed with `Cannot re-initialize CUDA in forked subprocess`.\n- **With the fix:** staging build [99622](https://buildkite.com/vllm/ci/builds/99622), same plan, same order on shard 5/7: all 7 shards passed. 42 passed / 1 skipped, the same counts and the same test IDs as a recent main build.\n- On main today the test passes only because no CUDA-initializing test runs before it in its shard.\n\n## Details\n\n- **Root cause:** `create_new_process_for_each_test()` defaults to fork on CUDA (`tests/utils.py`). `test_clone_elimination.py` creates a CUDA tensor in the pytest process, so a forked child of that process can't initialize CUDA. The failure depends on test order, not on depyf.\n- **Why spawn on the test, not on the step:** it fixes the test wherever it runs, and the same decorator argument is already used by the cudagraph and worker tests.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\nWritten with Claude Code; the human submitter reviews the changed line before merge.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
